(Regression test for bug #68's other half: the VARIABLE form of a hole over
 a `value`. Print learned to read a `value`'s shadow tag slot in stage 1e,
 but the buffer sinks never got the matching arm, so `a text called t is
 "{v}".` stored the payload as a decimal integer while `Print "{v}"` on the
 same variable was right. A `value` global keeps its tag in a BSS mirror
 rather than a stack slot, so both are exercised.

 A BARE name is a variable part and a QUOTED one is an expression part, so
 the two spellings take different paths: `chosen` was right in Print and
 wrong everywhere else, while `'the global one'` was wrong even in Print.
 Both are here. The same tag machinery serves the other tagged expression
 spellings - a mixed list's `last`, and a call to a function declared to
 give back a value - so they are checked too.

 Acceptance: Print and the text initializer agree, for a local `value`, for
 a global `value` reassigned inside a function, and for the two other
 tagged reads.)

a value called 'the global one' is nothing.
a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].

To 'set and show'.
  Set 'the global one' to element 2 of nested.
  Print "in a function: {'the global one'}".
  a text called seen is "captured there: {'the global one'}".
  Print seen.

a value called chosen is element 3 of nested.
Print "print: {chosen}".
a text called captured is "text: {chosen}".
Print captured.

'set and show'.
Print "at the top: {'the global one'}".

To 'the fourth thing'. Return a value, "four".
Print "last: {nested's last}".
a text called 'the last one' is "last: {nested's last}".
Print 'the last one'.
Print "called: {'the fourth thing'}".
a text called 'the called one' is "called: {'the fourth thing'}".
Print 'the called one'.
